                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "George Liu",
                        "email": "liuxiwei@ieisystem.com",
                        "username": "lxwinspur"
                    },
                    "message": "Unless necessary, we should use asynchronous calls:\n\n```\nboost::system::error_code getAllDbusObjects(\n    Context::ptr ctx, const std::string& serviceRoot,\n    const std::string& interface, const std::string& match,\n    ObjectTree& objectTree);\n```"
                },
                {
                    "file": "dcmihandler.cpp",
                    "line": 250,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Thang Tran",
                        "email": "thuutran@amperecomputing.com",
                        "username": "thangtran-ampere"
                    },
                    "message": "The writeAssetTagToFru function is a callback function of a timer, We can not pass the `Context::ptr ctx` to this function, therefore, we can not use `boost::system::error_code getAllDbusObjects...` method."
                },
                {
                    "file": "dcmihandler.cpp",
                    "line": 250,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "George Liu",
                        "email": "liuxiwei@ieisystem.com",
                        "username": "lxwinspur"
                    },
                    "message": "So this is due to the use of a timer, not a reason to use synchronization.\nI recommend using `boost::asio::steady_timer`.\n\n@vernon.mauery@gmail.com\nAny thoughts?"
                },
                {
                    "file": "dcmihandler.cpp",
                    "line": 289,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "George Liu",
                        "email": "liuxiwei@ieisystem.com",
                        "username": "lxwinspur"
                    },
                    "message": "```\nboost::system::error_code setDbusProperty(\n    Context::ptr ctx, const std::string& service, const std::string& objPath,\n    const std::string& interface, const std::string& property,\n    const Value& value);\n```"
                },
                {
